(a) the progress made under the Innovation in Science Pursuit for Inspired Research (INSPIRE) programme during the last five years, including the number of students and young researchers supported, component-wise;
(b) whether Government proposes to strengthen the programme to encourage meritorious students to pursue higher education and research in science;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to improve outreach and participation under the programme, particularly in rural, remote and aspirational districts?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM JANMAN) for the development of Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs);
(b) the key interventions in health, education, housing, connectivity and livelihood support provided to PVTG habitations; and
(c) the number of beneficiaries covered and infrastructure projects completed since the launch of the PM JANMAN scheme?

(a) whether preparatory activities for Census 2027, including House Listing and Housing Census, have commenced across all States and Union Territories;
(b) the State-wise status of digital infrastructure and self-enumeration facilities for Census, 2027;
(c) whether training programmes have been conducted for census functionaries and supervisors;
(d) whether any funds have been released to States and Union Territories for census-related activities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of beneficiaries covered under Ayushman Bharat-Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY);
(b) the number of Accredited Social Health Activists (ASHA), Anganwadi Workers (AWWs) and Anganwadi Helpers (AWHs) included in the scheme since February 2024;
(c) the number of hospitals, including private hospitals, empaneled under the scheme; and
(d) the total number of hospital admissions authorized under the scheme and its financial cost in the year 2025-26?

(a) the measures taken to safeguard India's petroleum and natural gas supply chains during recent geopolitical disruptions in West Asia;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any review of India's preparedness to manage disruptions in crude oil, LNG and petroleum product supplies;
(c) the steps taken to diversify import sources and strengthen strategic reserves, and;
(d) whether any long-term policy changes are proposed to enhance national energy security; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) extent of participation under National Youth Parliament Scheme (NYPS) 2.0 since its launch, including number of institutions registered, sittings conducted under each mode and participants enrolled through the portal;
(b) current status of implementation of the Consultative Committee Management System (CCMS), including number of Ministries and Consultative Committees onboarded thereon;
(c) steps taken to promote wider participation in the NYPS particularly among rural areas, smaller educational institutions and socially disadvantaged groups; 
(d) whether Government proposes to further strengthen the NYPS and CCMS through measures such as curriculum integration, capacity building and digital upgradation; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made by the Live Events Development Cell (LEDC) since its constitution, including the key outcomes of its four meetings held so far;
(b) the number of States/Union Territories that have adopted the Model Executive Order, 2026;
(c) the number of event-related permissions processed through the Single-Window Clearance System on the India Cine Hub (ICH) portal; and
(d) the steps taken to position India as a global hub for live events by 2030, including infrastructure and ease-of-doing-business measures for event organisers?
GK

(a) the progress achieved in developing domestic mineral processing, beneficiation and recycling capacity for key minerals, including critical and strategic minerals as of May, 2026;
(b) the details of new processing units, recycling facilities and value-addition infrastructure established under Government initiatives;
(c) whether integration of mineral beneficiation with downstream industries such as electronics, EVs and renewable energy has been undertaken;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the impact achieved in terms of import substitution, value addition and supply chain resilience?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the implementation of the Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan (DAJGUA) during 2026 and if so, the outcome thereof;
(b) the State-wise status of implementation of the interventions under the Abhiyan, including the number of tribal-majority villages covered, funds utilised and beneficiaries covered so far;
(c) whether Government has identified delays or shortfalls in implementation, utilisation of funds or convergence of schemes under the Abhiyan in any State or Union Territory; and
(d) if so, details thereof?

(a) the number of Jan Aushadhi Kendras (JAKs) opened across the country as of June 2026;
(b) the discount offered for drugs and surgical equipments at Jan Aushadhi Kendras as compared to branded medicines; and
(c) the sale made at Jan Aushadhi Kendras in the Financial Year 2025-26 and till June 2026 for the current Financial Year?

(a) the present status of implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas Karyakram (PMJVK), including number of projects sanctioned, completed and under implementation; 
(b) the details of infrastructure created under the Scheme, including educational institutions, health centres and skill development facilities; 
(c) whether convergence with State Governments and local bodies has been undertaken for selection and execution of projects; 
(d) if so, the details thereof; and 
(e) the impact achieved in terms of improved access to education, health and skill infrastructure in minority-concentrated areas?

(a) the progress made in implementation of the Viability Gap Funding scheme for Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS), including the storage capacity awarded and commissioned; 
(b) the measures taken to promote deployment of standalone and co-located battery storage projects for renewable energy integration, improve grid flexibility and enhance power reliability; 
(c) the role envisaged for BESS in meeting peak electricity demand and supporting grid reliability; and, 
(d) whether Government proposes additional policy regulatory or financial measures to accelerate the adoptive of energy storage technologies across the country; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made in implementing Carbon Capture, Utilisation and Storage (CCUS) initiatives in the petroleum and natural gas sector; 
(b) the refineries and upstream projects identified for pilot implementation; 
(c) the incentives and regulatory framework proposed to encourage private investment in CCUS technologies; and 
(d) the contribution envisaged from CCUS towards achieving India's climate commitments?

(a) current status of implementation of National e-Vidhan Application (NeVA) across the Houses of State Legislatures and the two Houses of Parliament; 
(b) extent to which NeVA and other digital parliamentary platforms have improved the efficiency of legislative business, including reduction in paperwork, processing time and administrative expenditure; 
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken to evaluate performance and impact of NeVA and allied digital platforms; 
(d) if so, the key findings thereof; 
(e) whether Government proposes to further strengthen these platforms, particularly with regard to accessibility, cybersecurity, interoperability and real-time coordination among stakeholders; and 
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has released the draft Telecommunications (Television, Radio and Associated Services) Rules, 2026 to consolidate multiple existing broadcasting guidelines into a single regulatory framework under the Telecommunications Act, 2023;
(b) if so, the key features proposed in these draft rules;
(c) whether timelines have been set for finalisation and implementation of the Rules; and 
(d) the measures proposed to support industry transition to the new regulatory framework?

(a) the objectives and salient provisions of the Scheme to Promote Manufacturing of Electric Passenger Cars in India (SPMEPCI), particularly in the context of attracting investment and promoting domestic manufacturing;
(b) whether the scheme has a provision for the localization of manufacturing and transfer of technology, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of the proposed investment, manufacturing capacity, and employment generation under the scheme; and
(d) the framework for the implementation of the scheme, including the role of the Central Government and the participating manufacturers?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana in creating modern food processing infrastructure and value addition facilities in all States including Maharashtra;
(b) the number of projects sanctioned, completed, and the employment generated through the scheme district-wise including Maharashtra;
(c) the steps taken to reduce post-harvest losses, promote farmer producer organisations, and enhance farmer income especially in the Khandesh and Marthwada rigion of Maharashtra; and
(d) the overall impact on food processing capacity, exports and growth of the sector?

(a) the progress made under the IndiaAI Mission till May 2026, including the initiatives launched pursuant to the India Artificial Intelligence (AI) Governance Guidelines;
(b) the status of development of indigenous AI foundation models, common compute infrastructure and AI datasets under the Mission;
(c) the measures taken to promote the adoption and development of artificial intelligence by Startups, Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) and academic institutions in the country including Uttar Pradesh; and
(d) the safeguards put in place to ensure responsible, transparent and secure deployment of AI technologies?

(a) the number and value of development partnership projects approved during the last one year through grants and Lines of Credit;
(b) the sectors covered under those projects;
(c) the progress made in introducing digital monitoring and outcome assessment of overseas development projects; and
(d) the proposed focus areas for India's development cooperation programme during 2026–27?

(a) the progress made under the LiFE (Lifestyle for Environment) Movement, so far;
(b) the key achievements in India’s climate action including Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs), renewable energy expansion and reduction of emission intensity;
(c) how these initiatives contribute towards India’s goal of becoming a developed nation with net-zero emissions by 2070; and
(d) the details of initiatives undertaken under the LiFE Movement, including in the State of Maharashtra?

(a) the progress made under Mission Mausam since its launch, including the major infrastructure and technological upgrades undertaken;
(b) the status of deployment of Doppler Weather Radars, upper-air observation systems/network and other weather monitoring infrastructure under the Mission;
(c) the measures taken to improve the forecasting and early warning systems for cyclones, heavy rainfall and other extreme weather events; and
(d) the roadmap for achieving panchayat-level weather forecasting and strengthening climate services under the Mission?
GK

(a) the progress made under the Prime Minister's Development Initiative for North East Region (PM-DevINE), including the projects approved, completed and under implementation, State-wise;
(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised under the scheme during financial year 2025–26 and funds allocated and released for financial year 2026–27;
(c) whether any new projects have been approved under PM-DevINE and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure timely implementation and outcome-based monitoring of projects under the scheme?

(a) the measures undertaken to strengthen the domestic production and processing of rare earth elements and 
magnets;
(b) the progress made in developing rare earth value chains through Indian Rare Earths Limited (IREL) and other agencies; 
(c) the details of steps taken to ensure supply chain resilience for strategic sectors such as electric vehicles, renewable energy and defence;
(d) whether Government has identified new projects or partnerships to reduce import dependence on rare earth materials; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to expand the skill development ecosystem in the country during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the progress of Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY);
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether PMKVY 4.0 has introduced any measure for improving quality and transparency in skill training; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the progress of construction of National High-Speed Corridors and Greenfield Expressways during 2026 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) State-wise status of ongoing and completed National High-Speed Corridor and Expressway projects, including the length awarded, under construction and completed so far;
(c) whether any measures have been taken to expedite completion of delayed highway and expressway projects through revised implementation mechanisms or contractual reforms; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Panchayat Devolution Index has been operationalised across all States and Union Territories;
(b) whether the Ministry has assessed the progress of States under the Index;
(c) whether the findings of the Index are being utilised for policy formulation and capacity building of Panchayati Raj Institutions;
(d) whether any incentive or support has been provided to improve performance under the Index; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and key components of the initiative for integrated development of 500 reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars announced in the Union Budget 2026–27;
(b) whether reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars have been identified for implementation of the initiative, if so, the criteria adopted therefor;
(c) the proposed coverage of Fish Farmer Producer Organisations (Fish FPOs), women-led groups and fisheries cooperatives under the initiative; and
(d) the planned investment, including the contribution of the Centre and the States, for implementation of the initiative?

(a) the funds released by the Ministry for State Annual Action Plans (SAAPs) since 2014-15;
(b) the number of Ayush Hospitals and Ayush Dispensaries that have been supported since 2014-15; and
(c) the number of Ayush Grams that have been supported by the Ministry since 2014-15?

(a) the present status of implementation of MSME Cluster Development Programme, including number of Common Facility Centres (CFCs) established and operational as of May 2026, State and district-wise including the State of Assam;
(b) the details of infrastructure created under cluster development projects, including testing labs, training centres and shared production facilities;
(c) whether integration of MSME clusters with supply chains, vendor networks and export-oriented production systems has been undertaken;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the impact achieved on value addition, employment generation and competitiveness of MSME clusters?

(a) the key features of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) 2.0 and the major changes that have been made in it as compared to the previous phase of the Mission;
(b) the implementation framework and funding pattern under the Mission;
(c) the reforms proposed to strengthen source sustainability, operation and maintenance of rural water supply systems and community participation;
(d) the State-wise funds allocated and released under JJM 2.0 during the year 2026-27; and
(e) the timeline and targets for achieving universal and sustainable rural household tap water supply under the Mission?

(a) the status of implementation of the Urban Challenge Fund (UCF), including the framework for project selection, funding pattern and progress achieved during Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) whether guidelines have been issued for selection of cities and projects under the UCF;
(c) the sectors proposed to be covered, including redevelopment of cities, water and sanitation infrastructure and urban mobility;
(d) the planned financial outlay, including the contribution of the Centre, States and other stakeholders; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote coal gasification and other cleaner coal technologies during 2026 including the State of Bihar;
(b) the number of coal gasification projects approved or under implementation, and their current status;
(c) whether any financial incentives or viability gap funding mechanisms have been introduced to support such projects, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the expected improvement in coal utilisation efficiency and reduction in emissions and enhancing domestic energy security through these technologies?
